{"path":"filesystem/filesystem_error/filesystem_error","title":"std::filesystem::filesystem_error::filesystem_error","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::filesystem::filesystem_error::</span>filesystem_error","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error/filesystem_error","section":"filesystem","kind":"page","summary":"Constructs a new filesystem_error object.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">filesystem_error<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> what_arg,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">filesystem_error<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> what_arg,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/path\"><span class=\"kw2219\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p1,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">filesystem_error<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> what_arg,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/path\"><span class=\"kw2219\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p1,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/path\"><span class=\"kw2219\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p2,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">filesystem_error<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> filesystem_error<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Constructs a new <code>filesystem_error</code> object.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> The error code is set to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec</span></code> and optionally, the paths that were involved in the operation that resulted in the error, are set to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p1</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p2</span></code>. <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error/what\"><code>what()</code></a> after construction returns a string that contains <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">what_arg</span></code> (assuming that it does not contain an embedded null character ). If either or both <code>path</code> arguments are not provided, a null <code>path</code> is used instead.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Copy constructor. Initialize the contents with those of <code>other</code>. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> both have dynamic type <code>std::filesystem_error::filesystem_error</code> then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strcmp\"><span class=\"kw1154\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strcmp</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>what<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, other.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> what_arg\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> explanatory string\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> error code for the specific operating system dependent error\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p1, p2\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> paths involved in the operation raising system error\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another <code>filesystem_error</code> object to copy\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Because copying <code>std::filesystem::filesystem_error</code> is not permitted to throw exceptions, the explanatory string is typically stored internally in a separately-allocated reference-counted storage. This is also why there is no constructor taking <code>std::string&amp;&amp;</code>: it would have to copy the content anyway.\n</p><p>Typical implementations also store <code>path</code> objects referenced by <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error/path\">path1()</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error/path\">path2()</a></span> in the reference-counted storage.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"filesystem","title":"Filesystem library (since C++17)"},{"path":"filesystem/filesystem_error","title":"std::filesystem::filesystem_error"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::filesystem::filesystem_error::filesystem_error","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++17. Constructs a new filesystem_error object."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"what_arg, ec, p1, p2, other"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Because copying std::filesystem::filesystem_error is not permitted to throw exceptions, the explanatory string is typically stored internally in a…"},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":237,"codeBlockCount":0}
